# ═══════════════════════════════════════════
# Crypto Idea — Environment Variables
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NEVER commit .env to git (it's in .gitignore)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════

# Firebase (from Firebase Console → Project Settings → Web App)
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=crypto-idea.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=crypto-idea
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=crypto-idea.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_sender_id_here
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_app_id_here

# CoinGecko API key — NOT set here. The key lives on the BACKEND (the /api proxy
# Cloud Function) so it stays secret and requests are cached/shared across users.
# Set COINGECKO_DEMO_KEY in functions/.env (see functions/.env.example) for BOTH
# the emulator and production. `firebase functions:config:set` no longer exists —
# it was removed in firebase-functions v7, which this project is on.
# Put it in functions/.env rather than the admin Settings panel: only the env var
# unlocks full history (days=max); the Settings value lifts rate limits but leaves
# DCA history clamped to 365 days. Get a free Demo key at coingecko.com/en/api.

# App Check (bot protection) — reCAPTCHA v3 site key from Firebase Console → App Check.
# When set (production), the app sends App Check tokens with Auth/Firestore/Functions calls.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=

# (Admin is now a Firebase custom claim, not an email list — VITE_ADMIN_EMAILS is unused.)
